 "stale": false,
 "narrative": "Hay movement and demand remained steady across the state this past week as producers continued finishing up final alfalfa cuttings, which appear to be of very high quality. Harvest activities have wrapped up or are nearing completion in most areas. Grass hay movement also remained steady, with strong demand for high-quality small square bales. According to the US Drought Monitor for the week of November 19th, only targeted changes in drought classification were made over the High Plains states this past week. A small degradation occurred in the Northern Colorado Rockies with a couple small degradations in Eastern Kansas.  In Kansas, the categorical percent area of abnormally dry conditions (D0) increased to 25%, Moderate drought (D1) decreased to 10%, severe drought (D2) stayed at 2%, and there was no extreme drought (D3) or exceptional drought (D4) recorded with 63% of the state experiencing no drought. Prices below reflect the average price. There could be prices higher and lower prices than those published. Happy Thanksgiving!\n\nRFV Chart\nAlfalfa Quality Guidelines  \nQuality       ADF           NDF        *RFV/RFQ       **TDN-100%      **TDN-90%        CP \nSupreme     <27          <34         >185                  >62                       >55.9              >22 \nPremium     27-29     34-36       170-185           60.5-62                54.5-55.9        20-22 \nGood            29-32     36-40       150-170           58-60                   52.5-54.5        18-20 \nFair               32-35    40-44        130-150           56-58                   50.5-52.5        16-18 \nUtility            >35         >44            <130               <56                        <50.5              <16  \n*RFV calculated using the Wis/Minn formula. **TDN calculated using the Western formula. Quantitative factors are approximate, and many factors can affect feeding value. Values based on 100% dry matter (TDN showing both 100% & 90%). Guidelines are to be used with visual appearance and intent of sale (usage).",
 "source": "USDA AMS Market News",
 "source_url": "https://mymarketnews.ams.usda.gov/viewReport/2885",
